</div>

<!-- SECTION 1: GLOBAL OVERVIEW -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <div class="section-num">1</div>
    <div>
      <div class="section-title">Global Homicide Rate Overview</div>
      <div class="section-objective">Overall global trend in homicide rates from 1990 to 2023, including reporting coverage and key trajectory findings.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="body-text">The global median intentional homicide rate has followed a non-linear trajectory over the 33-year observation window. From a peak in the early 1990s — driven partly by post-Cold War instability and expanding reporting — rates declined through the 2000s and 2010s before partially stabilising in the 2020s. In 2023, the global median rate stood at <strong>{global_median:.2f} per 100,000</strong>, while the mean of <strong>{global_mean:.2f}</strong> reflects a right-skewed distribution dominated by high-rate outliers.</p>

  <div class="insight-box success">
    <strong>Headline finding:</strong> The global mean homicide rate declined approximately 9.6% from the 2000s to the 2010s, suggesting measurable progress in public safety — though the 2020s show signs of stagnation and the disparity across regions remains stark.
  </div>

  <div class="chart-container tall">
    <canvas id="globalTrendChart"></canvas>
  </div>

  <div class="decade-row">
    <div class="decade-card">
      <div class="decade-label">1990s Average</div>
